<title>BELGIUM: Belgium raises liquidity at money tender.</title>
<headline>Belgium raises liquidity at money tender.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian central bank raised money market liquidity at its fixed-rate tender for seven-day advances. Details -</p>
<p>    Value date 12/02	  expiry on 19/02    NBVA</p>
<p>    Amount allotted	   10.000 bln bfr    (9.975 bln *)</p>
<p>    Interest rate	     3.00 pct	    (3.00 pct **)</p>
<p>    Total amount of bids    17.175 bln bfr</p>
<p>Percentage of bids accepted  57.7</p>
<p>* amount draining from the money market on February 12</p>
<p>** interest rate at previous tender on February 3</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
